WEBVTT

00:10:28.172 --> 00:10:30.033
LR: Behavioral questions are generally,

00:10:30.057 --> 00:10:33.444
"Tell me about a time when you were
in this situation and what you did."

00:10:33.468 --> 00:10:36.238
Woman 1: Tell me about a time
when you had a task or a goal

00:10:36.262 --> 00:10:37.422
that seemed impossible.

00:10:37.446 --> 00:10:40.501
Man 1: Tell me about a time
when you struggled to take criticism.

00:10:40.525 --> 00:10:43.225
Woman 2: Tell me about a time
when you ate a fruit salad.

00:10:43.249 --> 00:10:46.404
LR: And the idea is that past behavior
can predict future behavior,

00:10:46.428 --> 00:10:48.809
but you can still really easily game them

00:10:48.833 --> 00:10:53.297
when they are obvious
questions about, you know,

00:10:53.321 --> 00:10:55.440
"Tell me about an ethical
decision you made,"

00:10:55.464 --> 00:10:56.629
and things like this.

00:10:57.241 --> 00:10:59.483
AG: It's easy for candidates
to choose a story

00:10:59.507 --> 00:11:01.594
that casts them
in the best possible light.